    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "A walk down Pattaya Walking Street can be an incredible experience. The neon lights and colour, music and noise, performers and people, food and odours, and everything else about this kilometre long road will dazzle you.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Some find it bliss, others numbing. But even if you are not into partying and prefer quiet places, you should consider visiting Thailand’s wildest walking street at least once.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Timings & Getting There",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The street is closed to vehicles from 7:00 pm – 3:00 am. By 8:00 pm most places are open, but there isn’t much action before 10:00 pm. Walking Street Pattaya comes alive around midnight.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "The distance from Central Pattaya to Walking Street is about 1.2 miles (2 km). To get here, you can either walk along the beach or take a shared open-air tuk-tuk (songthaew) that takes rounds of the city.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Watch a Band Perform",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The live bands performing in Walking Street Pattaya are amazing. On any night there should be at least 5 bands playing. You can walk along the street, find a band you like (you’ll be able to see and hear bands play from the road), and enjoy drinks while tapping your feet or dancing to popular songs.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Sipping on a 100 Baht ($3) beer in a bar while watching a live performance is our favourite thing to do in Thailand’s Walking Streets. Performers in the area are exceptionally talented – so whichever bar you select, you’ll get to enjoy a great performance.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Enjoy a Sumptuous Meal",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The Walking Street in Pattaya has excellent food options. In addition to open air food stalls, the street also has well-established restaurants that specialise in sea food. Some of these have dining areas that look out across Pattaya Bay, making them a great place to enjoy a meal while taking a break from the hustle and bustle.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Walking Street Pattaya Recommended Restaurants:",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Marine Sea Food: Centre of Walking Street. Inexpensive and basic restaurant serving delicious Thai food and fresh sea food.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "King Sea Food: Opposite Soi 14, Walking Street. Great view of the bay, good food and ambiance.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "La Notte Pub & Restaurant: 220/2-4, Walking Street. Serves delicious French and European cuisine.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Karma Indian Restaurant: 109/4 Moo 10, near Soi 15. One of the best Indian food restaurants in Pattaya.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Rasputin Restaurant Pattaya: 280/1, near the Bali Hai end of the street. Stylish and lively Russian restaurant with a good selection of dishes.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "L’Italiano Italian Restaurant: 94/7 Moo 10, Walking Street. Extensive menu with an impressive wine selection.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You can also sample delicious street food and try exotic Thai fruits. The Turkish ice cream shop here is famous all over Pattaya.",
            "url": "https://toasttothailand.com/things-to-do/exotic-thai-fruits/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://toasttothailand.com/things-to-do/exotic-thai-fruits/",
                "anchor_text": "try exotic Thai fruits"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Experience Pattaya’s Nightlife",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "When it comes to nightlife, Pattaya Walking Street is king. The street has venues, bars, nightclubs, and go-go bars to suit every taste. You’ll see flashy neon signs advertising bars everywhere. Women holding placards, displaying the rates of beer, will invite you to their nightclubs.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Some clubs like the Moulin Rouge have scantily clad women appearing behind windows – and so, you’ll see plenty of “window shopping” in the area. In all, there are over 100 night clubs and go-go bars in Walking Street Pattaya. Here is a list of top night clubs and go-go bars on the street.",
            "url": "http://www.bangkok.com/pattaya/nightlife/pattaya-walking-street-bars.htm",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://www.bangkok.com/pattaya/nightlife/pattaya-walking-street-bars.htm",
                "anchor_text": "top night clubs"
              },
              {
                "url": "http://www.bangkok.com/pattaya/nightlife/pattaya-walking-street-go-go-bars.htm",
                "anchor_text": "go-go bars"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Keep in mind: If you visit gentlemen’s clubs and go-go bars, you’ll end up paying a lot more than the advertised rate.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Watch The World Go By (People Watching)",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You’ll see hundreds of people from all over the world, trying to make sense of their surroundings. Some are seeing a walking street in Thailand for the first time and the culture shock on their faces show. (This can be quite amusing to watch). Some come to have a good time and enjoy drinks, others for the women.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Sitting in a bar with a good view of the street – such as Frog Bar – and enjoying a beer, while watching the world go by can also be a fun thing to do here.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Though the matches are partly staged and not as vicious as the real thing, they are still fun to watch. You can even step in the ring to test your boxing skills and get photographed with the boxers (a tip will be expected).",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Watch a Muay Thai Show",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You’ll also get to see Muay Thai boxing shows on Pattaya Walking Street. The most popular one is about halfway down the street, opposite the entrance to Marine Plaza.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Visit the Bal Hai Pier (Pattaya Pier)",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "On one end of the street is the Pattaya Pier – a central feature of the city. Ferries to Koh Larn Island leave from here.",
            "url": "https://toasttothailand.com/pattaya-things-to-do/koh-larn-coral-island/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://toasttothailand.com/pattaya-things-to-do/koh-larn-coral-island/",
                "anchor_text": "Koh Larn Island"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "If the noise and commotion of the road gets too much for you, Pattaya Pier is a good place to take a break. The pier is pretty and quiet at night. It’s a great place to enjoy a beer in silence before you head back.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "What Not to do in Walking Street Pattaya",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "As long as you behave responsibly and act reasonably, you should have lots of fun exploring the street. However, keep the following points in mind:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Don’t go for Sex Shows",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Whether you visit with your partner or alone, touts will approach you and ask if you would like to watch a sex show. They will be carrying a menu with women on it. Even if you are curious, going for a sex show is a bad idea. You will most likely be ripped off. People fall into this trap and regret it.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Don’t Display Your Money",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "In general, Thailand’s walking streets have a few pickpockets. Be careful whenever you pull out your wallet to make payments, and always count the change you get back. Avoid carrying valuables.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "(In 2019, when we last visited Pattaya Walking Street a decently dressed man approached us and asked us to visit his night club. We told him that we were not interested. But he continued to be friendly – even though he didn’t really seem interested in us. We took this as a warning and asked him to stay away. And, sure enough – although we were extra alert, by then he had somehow managed to unbutton the pocket my wallet was in and pull it out halfway. It could have been a sad end to an amazing holiday. Pickpockets here are very skilled so be alert).",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Don’t do Drugs",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You might be approached by someone offering or selling drugs. Stay away. It could be a setup. Drugs in Thailand are illegal and the consequences of being in possession are very serious.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Don’t Forget to Stay in Your Senses",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Don’t get carried away by the ambiance and festive mood of this wild nightlife area in Pattaya. We have seen people get so drunk that they do not even remember where their hotel is. This can be a disaster. Drink responsibly.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Also, the chances of getting mugged are far greater when you are drunk. So stay alert. (Our article on keeping safe in Thailand covers other points to keep in mind when visiting areas such as Thailand’s walking streets).",
            "url": "https://toasttothailand.com/planning-your-trip/common-scams-staying-safe/",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://toasttothailand.com/planning-your-trip/common-scams-staying-safe/",
                "anchor_text": "keeping safe in Thailand"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Don’t Disrespect Women",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Please don’t disrespect the women that work in Thailand’s walking streets and other such areas. Most of them have a tough life and they have no other option than to do what they do to support their families.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Hotels near Walking Street Pattaya",
        "main_title": "Pattaya Walking Street: Thailand’s Most Famous Walking Street",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "If you can handle the music from bars (and prefer not to find your way back to your hotel late at night), then booking accommodation in or near the walking street is a good option. You’ll need to book in advance.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
